    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green (45 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, with every value derived from it flowing to the new identity.\n\n**Core change \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode.java`**\n- Replaced the old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` city-sequence format with `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n  - **REGION** = region code derived from the postcode via `Locality.of(city, postcode)` (postcode range first, city table fallback, `UNKNOWN` otherwise).\n  - **HASH8** = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`. Since this step runs after telephone normalization and `BuildOwner`, `owner.getTelephone()` is the stored E.164 value \u2014 matching what the tests recompute from the response.\n- Dropped the sequence logic entirely; the step no longer needs `OwnerRepository`.\n\n**Values built from `customerCode` \u2014 moved automatically to the new identity**\n- **Membership number** (`AssignMembershipNumber`) and **check digit** (`CheckDigit`, Luhn over the code's digits) already derive from `customerCode`, so they now compute over the region-and-hash value with no logic change (doc example refreshed).\n- **Create audit record** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) logs `customerCode`, so audit lines now carry the new identity (confirmed in test output, e.g. `customerCode=NSW-11DE574F`).\n\n**Locality derivation \u2014 explicitly moved onto the identity**\n- `Locality.of(Owner)` now reads the REGION prefix from `customerCode` so locality and identity always agree, falling back to the direct postcode/city derivation only when no `customerCode` is present (e.g. seed records). Wired into `OwnerMapper`.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated the `openapi.yml` descriptions/examples for `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality`.\n\nAll identity checkpoints (Cp09/13/14/16/17/21/29/30/31/32) and the full 45-test suite pass.",
